# Lesson 2, new hand: partner opens 2NT, you have 5. Student sits South.
title: Partner opens 2NT, you have 5
id: L02-23
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.4
student: S
board: 45
dealer: N
vulnerable: both

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  AQ5    AK73   KQ4    KJ6
  E  K9762  J64    A85    43
  S  J84    Q52    9763   Q85
  W  T3     T98    JT2    AT972

auction:
  N 2NT    = 21-22 points, balanced
  E Pass
  S 3NT*   = 4+ points: game
     key: 5 HCP opposite 21-22 makes at least 26. Bid game.
     not Pass: Did you count 5? With 4 or more opposite 2NT, raise to game.
     not *: With 4+ points opposite 2NT, the lesson says raise to 3NT.
  W Pass
  N Pass
  E Pass

auction recap:
  Partner's 2NT showed 21-22 points and a balanced hand. Your 5 points
  bring your side to at least 26, so you bid game. North is declarer,
  because she bid no-trump first, and so East will lead to the first
  trick.

play:
  1   E S6  S S4  W ST  N SQ
  2   N CJ  E C3  S C5  W CA
      note: Declarer's plan: drive out the ♣A, then take hearts, spades, clubs and a diamond. Dummy's two queens help.
  3   W DJ  N DQ  E DA  S D3
  4   E C4  S C8  W C9  N CK
  5   N H3  E H4  S HQ  W H8
      note: Now the hearts. Dummy's ♥Q first, the high card from the short side.
  6   S H2  W H9  N HK  E H6
      note: Back to declarer's ♥K.
  7   N HA  E HJ  S H5  W HT
      note: And the ♥A.
  8   N H7  E S2  S D6  W S3
      note: The hearts split evenly, so the last one is a winner.
  9   N C6  E S7  S CQ  W C2
      note: A club to dummy's ♣Q.
  10  S D7  W D2  N DK  E D5
      note: Back to declarer's ♦K.
  11  N SA  E S9  S S8  W C7
      note: The ♠A.
  12  N S5  E SK  S SJ  W DT
      note: Ten tricks are in. East's ♠K takes this one.
  13  E D8  S D9  W CT  N D4
      note: 10 tricks: 3NT made with an overtrick.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: drive out the ♣A, then take the hearts, spades, clubs
  and a diamond.

  3NT made with an overtrick. Your ♥Q, ♣Q and last diamond all became
  tricks: even a few points matter opposite a 2NT opener.
